      "summary": "Positano: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 1: Positano: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Positano - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/positano-character.jpg)\n\nPositano clings dramatically to the vertical limestone cliffs of the Amalfi Peninsula, cascading toward the sparkling Tyrrhenian Sea in a sun-drenched avalanche of pink, peach, and terracotta villas. Steep stone stairways called scalinatelle take the place of streets, winding through fragrant pergolas of purple bougainvillea and terraced lemon groves laden with heavy citrus fruit.\n\n![Geographic location of Positano in Italy](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/positano-map.png)\n\nAt the base of the cliffs lies the dark volcanic sand of the Spiaggia Grande, where colorful wooden fishing boats rest alongside rows of striped parasols. The majolica tiled dome of the Church of Santa Maria Assunta glitters in green and gold against the azure water. At twilight, hundreds of villa windows and terrace lanterns illuminate the cliffside, transforming the vertical village into a glowing constellation suspended between mountain and sea."
