      "summary": "Kotor: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 3: Kotor: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Kotor - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/kotor-character.jpg)\n\nTucked away at the deepest recess of the breathtaking Bay of Kotor, this fortified jewel is embraced by sheer gray limestone mountains that drop straight into fjord-like waters. Four kilometers of ancient Venetian walls zig-zag impossibly up the vertical rock face of Saint John's Hill, crowned by an ancient stone fortress surveying the serpentine gulf below.\n\n![Geographic location of Kotor in Montenegro](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/kotor-map.png)\n\nWithin the sea gates lies a labyrinthine medieval town paved in polished gray marble, filled with Romanesque churches, Renaissance palaces, and quiet squares frequented by the city's beloved stray cats. The twin stone belfries of Saint Tryphon's Cathedral rise dramatically against the sheer limestone precipice behind them, creating an intimate, fortress-like sanctuary where Mediterranean sea breezes meet rugged Balkan highlands."
