      "summary": "Rovinj: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 4: Rovinj: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Rovinj - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/rovinj-character.jpg)\n\nRovinj rises from the crystalline waters of the northern Adriatic like a teardrop of stone, its ancient pastel houses packed tightly on an egg-shaped peninsula. The town's narrow, winding alleys are paved with polished white limestone flagstones, worn smooth by centuries of fishermen's footsteps and maritime sea salt.\n\n![Geographic location of Rovinj in Croatia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/rovinj-map.png)\n\nAt the peninsula's highest crest stands the grand baroque Church of Saint Euphemia, its sixty-meter bell tower modeled directly after the Campanile of Saint Mark in Venice. At the harbor quays, traditional wooden batana fishing boats with colorful sails bob in the clear water. As dusk settles, seaside bars place cushions directly on the smooth rock shelves over the waves, offering front-row seats to fiery Adriatic sunsets."
