      "summary": "Portofino: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 5: Portofino: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Portofino - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/portofino-character.jpg)\n\nTucked into a protected inlet along the rugged Ligurian coast, Portofino is the jewel of the Italian Riviera. A tight crescent of tall, slender houses painted in cheerful shades of ochre, terracotta, and olive green wraps around a tranquil harbor where luxury yachts moor alongside traditional wooden gozzi fishing vessels.\n\n![Geographic location of Portofino in Italy](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/portofino-map.png)\n\nOlive groves, maritime pines, and cypress trees carpet the steep headlands framing the cove. Cobblestone paths climb through pine-scented air toward the stone ramparts of Castello Brown and the tiny Church of San Giorgio, opening up breathtaking panoramas across the Gulf of Tigullio. In the quiet piazzetta by the water's edge, outdoor café tables catch the warm evening glow reflected on the emerald lagoon."
