      "summary": "Riomaggiore: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 6: Riomaggiore: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Riomaggiore - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/riomaggiore-character.jpg)\n\nRiomaggiore is the eastern gateway to the legendary Cinque Terre, squeezed dramatically into a narrow mountain gorge that spills down to a tiny rocky harbor. Traditional Ligurian tower houses—built three and four stories tall to maximize scarce vertical space—are painted in bright pink, ochre, and saffron, their stone foundations rooted directly into the steep valley walls.\n\n![Geographic location of Riomaggiore in Italy](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/riomaggiore-map.png)\n\nAbove the village, thousands of kilometers of dry-stone walls support ancient terraced vineyards producing crisp Sciacchetrà wine. Colorful wooden fishing skiffs are hauled up the steep paved slipway away from stormy waves. Looking back from the rocky sea breakwater, the entire village appears like an intricate vertical puzzle of vibrant facades illuminated by the setting sun."
