      "title": "Bonifacio: The Maritime Haven",
      "summary": "Bonifacio: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 7: Bonifacio: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Bonifacio - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/bonifacio-character.jpg)\n\nPerched precariously upon a narrow peninsula of dazzling white limestone, Bonifacio sits high above the churning Strait of Bonifacio at the southern tip of Corsica. Centuries of relentless sea spray and howling winds have undercut the chalky cliffs, leaving centuries-old stone ramparts and houses appearing to hover directly over crashing turquoise waves seventy meters below.\n\n![Geographic location of Bonifacio in France](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/bonifacio-map.png)\n\nBehind the citadel walls, dark cobblestone passageways, arched aqueducts, and ancient stone churches evoke a fiercely independent maritime history. The famous King of Aragon's Staircase features one hundred and eighty-seven steep steps carved directly into the vertical cliff face down to the sea. Below the cliffs, a fjord-like natural goulet shelters a lively marina where sailing yachts dock under the shadow of monumental limestone bastions."
