      "title": "Valletta: The Maritime Haven",
      "summary": "Valletta: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 8: Valletta: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Valletta - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/valletta-character.jpg)\n\nFounded in 1566 by the Knights of Saint John following the Great Siege of Malta, Valletta was conceived as an impregnable fortress city built by gentlemen for gentlemen. Enclosed within colossal honey-colored limestone bastions, the city is laid out in a strict grid of steep streets that plunge toward the sparkling waters of the Grand Harbour and Marsamxett Harbour.\n\n![Geographic location of Valletta in Malta](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/valletta-map.png)\n\nThe golden stone facades are distinguished by colorful wooden covered balconies called gallariji, painted in vibrant red, green, and navy blue. Inside Saint John's Co-Cathedral, the plain fortress exterior gives way to an astonishing explosion of high baroque gold leaf, intricately carved marble tombstones, and Caravaggio's masterpiece, The Beheading of Saint John the Baptist. From the Upper Barrakka Gardens, the view across the harbor toward the fortified Three Cities is one of the most majestic naval panoramas in Europe."
