      "title": "Piran: The Maritime Haven",
      "summary": "Piran: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 9: Piran: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Piran - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/piran-character.jpg)\n\nPiran stretches like a slender finger of terracotta tiles into the northern Adriatic Sea, serving as Slovenia's most picturesque coastal treasure. The historic town grew wealthy through centuries of trading sea salt harvested from the nearby Sečovlje salt pans, a heritage that financed elegant Venetian Gothic palaces and paved piazzas.\n\n![Geographic location of Piran in Slovenia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/piran-map.png)\n\nThe heart of the town is Tartini Square, a spacious oval marble plaza named after the baroque composer Giuseppe Tartini, whose bronze statue surveys the surrounding pastel facades. Climbing the narrow stone alleys leads to the hilltop Church of Saint George, where the bell tower offers sweeping views across the Adriatic toward the distant Italian coast and the snow-capped Julian Alps."
