      "title": "Nafplio: The Maritime Haven",
      "summary": "Nafplio: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 10: Nafplio: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Nafplio - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/nafplio-character.jpg)\n\nNestled on the calm Argolic Gulf, Nafplio served as the proud first capital of newly independent Greece in the 1820s. Overlooking the town is the colossal Palamidi Fortress, an eighteenth-century Venetian defensive masterpiece crowning a sheer two-hundred-meter rocky crest reached by nine hundred and ninety-nine stone steps.\n\n![Geographic location of Nafplio in Greece](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/nafplio-map.png)\n\nDown along the harbor, the tiny fortified islet of Bourtzi floats like a stone ship in the middle of the bay. The historic Old Town is a romantic tapestry of narrow pedestrian streets lined with neoclassical mansions, bougainvillea-draped stone balconies, and quiet paved squares shaded by citrus trees. Sunset over the gulf bathes the Venetian stone battlements in deep golden hues, highlighting its enduring Mediterranean grace."
