      "title": "San Sebastián: The Maritime Haven",
      "summary": "San Sebastián: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 11: San Sebastián: The Maritime Haven\n\n![San Sebastián - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/san-sebastian-character.jpg)\n\nSan Sebastián (Donostia in Basque) is the crown jewel of the Cantabrian coast, famous for the sweeping crescent curve of La Concha beach. Royal nineteenth-century patronage transformed the town into a summer paradise of Belle Époque promenades, ornate stone streetlamps, and grand seaside hotels facing the emerald Atlantic waters.\n\n![Geographic location of San Sebastián in Spain](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/san-sebastian-map.png)\n\nIn the historic Parte Vieja (Old Town) nestled beneath Mount Urgull, narrow streets are packed with world-renowned pintxo bars, where countertops overflow with culinary art featuring fresh seafood, Iberian ham, and wild mushrooms. Atlantic rollers crash against the dramatic wind-comb sculptures of Eduardo Chillida at the foot of Mount Igueldo, celebrating the rugged spirit of the Basque coast."
