      "title": "Villefranche-sur-Mer: The Maritime Haven",
      "summary": "Villefranche-sur-Mer: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 12: Villefranche-sur-Mer: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Villefranche-sur-Mer - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/villefranche-sur-mer-character.jpg)\n\nNestled between the rocky promontories of Mont Boron and Cap Ferrat, Villefranche-sur-Mer boasts one of the deepest natural harbors in the Mediterranean. The Old Town rises steeply from the water's edge in a glorious cascade of sunny ochre, warm peach, and deep apricot facades with louvered shutters and wrought-iron balconies.\n\n![Geographic location of Villefranche-sur-Mer in France](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/villefranche-sur-mer-map.png)\n\nA unique historical feature is the Rue Obscure, a vaulted fourteenth-century underground street running beneath the houses for defense against artillery fire. Along the quayside, outdoor café terraces overlook small fishing boats bobbing in waters of astonishing clarity. At the entrance to the harbor, the sixteenth-century Saint Elme Citadel stands with monumental stone ramparts, guarding centuries of peaceful maritime beauty."
