      "summary": "Funchal: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 14: Funchal: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Funchal - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/funchal-character.jpg)\n\nThe capital of Madeira rises like a vast natural amphitheater from the blue Atlantic Ocean, climbing steep volcanic slopes carpeted in lush gardens, banana plantations, and terraced vineyards. In the historic Zona Velha, cobblestone alleys are famous for the Painted Doors Project, where local artists have transformed dozens of vintage doorways into vibrant murals.\n\n![Geographic location of Funchal in Portugal](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/funchal-map.png)\n\nHigh above the harbor in Monte, exotic botanical gardens showcase flowering orchids, giant ferns, and jacaranda blossoms from around the globe. Traditional wicker toboggans steered by two men in white linen glide thrillingly down the steep asphalt hills. Down at the Mercado dos Lavradores, stalls overflow with exotic passion fruit, orchids, and fresh Atlantic tuna, celebrating the island's eternal springtime warmth."
