      "summary": "Saint-Malo: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 16: Saint-Malo: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Saint-Malo - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/saint-malo-character.jpg)\n\nRising from the rocky coast of northern Brittany, Saint-Malo is a historic walled citadel of austere gray granite, famous for its legacy of privateers, navigators, and explorers. A continuous circuit of thick stone ramparts encircles the historic town, offering breathtaking views across wide sandy beaches and offshore fortresses.\n\n![Geographic location of Saint-Malo in France](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/saint-malo-map.png)\n\nThe Bay of Saint-Malo experiences some of the greatest tidal ranges in Europe, with the ocean rising and falling up to twelve meters in a single day, transforming islands into dry peninsulas at low tide. Within the granite walls, tall slate-roofed mansions, cozy crêperies, and cobblestone lanes buzz with seafaring pride, standing as an enduring symbol of Breton independence."
