      "summary": "Valparaíso: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 17: Valparaíso: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Valparaíso - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/valparaiso-character.jpg)\n\nKnown as the 'Jewel of the Pacific,' Valparaíso cascades anarchically over forty-two steep coastal hills that plunge directly toward a bustling maritime harbor. Houses are constructed from wood and clad in corrugated iron painted in every vivid hue of the rainbow, creating an explosion of color across the steep hillside amphitheater.\n\n![Geographic location of Valparaíso in Chile](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/valparaiso-map.png)\n\nHistoric wooden funiculars called ascensores, dating from the late nineteenth century, rattle up sheer inclines to link the port with bohemian hill quarters like Cerro Alegre and Cerro Concepción. Labyrinthine stairways, cobblestone lanes, and street murals turn the city into an open-air art gallery, immortalized by Chilean poet Pablo Neruda from his quirky clifftop home, La Sebastiana."
