      "summary": "Paraty: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 18: Paraty: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Paraty - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/paraty-character.jpg)\n\nNestled along Brazil's lush Costa Verde between Rio and São Paulo, Paraty was the historic terminus of the Caminho do Ouro (Gold Trail), through which inland gold and diamonds were shipped to Portugal in the eighteenth century. Its historic center is closed to all motor vehicles, preserving an immaculate colonial grid of whitewashed stone buildings.\n\n![Geographic location of Paraty in Brazil](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/paraty-map.png)\n\nDuring full moon high tides, seawater gently floods the lower stone streets, washing them clean and reflecting colonial facades and colorful window frames like a miniature Venice. Surrounding the town are emerald rainforest mountains of the Serra da Bocaina and an archipelago of sixty-five tropical islands and secluded beaches, blending Portuguese heritage with tropical wilderness."
