      "title": "Salvador da Bahia: The Maritime Haven",
      "summary": "Salvador da Bahia: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 19: Salvador da Bahia: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Salvador da Bahia - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/salvador-da-bahia-character.jpg)\n\nThe first colonial capital of Brazil, Salvador perches on a triangular peninsula separating the Atlantic Ocean from the immense Bay of All Saints. The city is split dramatically into two levels: the Lower City along the harbor, and the Upper City anchored by the historic Pelourinho district, linked by the towering art deco Elevador Lacerda.\n\n![Geographic location of Salvador da Bahia in Brazil](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/salvador-da-bahia-map.png)\n\nIn the Pelourinho, cobblestone squares are lined with seventeenth- and eighteenth-century pastel colonial mansions in bright blue, yellow, and salmon. The Church of São Francisco features an interior encrusted in hundreds of kilograms of gold leaf. Salvador is the beating heart of Afro-Brazilian culture, where the hypnotic rhythms of Olodum drumming, the acrobatics of capoeira, and the aromas of dendê palm oil fill the tropical air."
