      "summary": "Willemstad: The Maritime Haven - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 2",
      "content": "### Chapter 20: Willemstad: The Maritime Haven\n\n![Willemstad - Iconic coastal view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/willemstad-character.jpg)\n\nThe capital of Curaçao presents one of the most delightful architectural curiosities in the Caribbean: authentic seventeenth-century Dutch canal houses transplanted to a tropical island. Along the Handelskade waterfront in the Punda district, traditional stepped and neck gables are painted in vibrant Caribbean shades of mango yellow, bright turquoise, coral pink, and cobalt.\n\n![Geographic location of Willemstad in Curaçao](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-02/images/willemstad-map.png)\n\nThe two historic waterfront districts are linked across the deep Saint Anna Bay by the Queen Emma Bridge, a unique floating pontoon bridge that swings open several times daily to let ocean freighters enter the port. Across the bay in Otrobanda, quiet residential lanes reveal pastel colonial courtyards and vibrant street murals, creating a joyous fusion of European heritage and Caribbean soul."
